From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:24:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/24] Save power on USB-C chargers on ASUS ROG Zephyrus
 laptops

The ACPI adapter reads online for the barrel and for a USB-C charger
alike, so a 100 W USB-C charger got the AC profile, performance. Read the
firmware's charge_mode (asus-armoury, or asus-nb-wmi on older kernels)
and treat USB-C as its own source: balanced by default, with the profile
picked there remembered apart from the barrel's.

Backport to v4.5.0-rc1: as on quattro; the new unit is the last entry of
first-run's per-unit enable loop.

